(:include "reach.domain")

// Shared tier: melee a target. First free yourself (one fix per plan), then close in, juke and hit.
//
// Teaches: a "fix-up ladder" (first match: the first thing in the way is fixed, the plan ends with it, the next
// replan takes the next rung), the target picked by a host sensor and handed down as a parameter.
// Source: Space Station 14 (MIT), `MeleeCombatCompound`, `BeforeMeleeAttackTargetCompound`,
// `MeleeAttackTargetCompound` and `EscapeCompound` in Resources/Prototypes/NPCs/Combat/melee.yml, and the
// `NearbyMeleeTargets` utility query, at commit 614f030530578e248a2393dd71ee9813d68d800d:
// https://github.com/space-wizards/space-station-14/blob/614f030530578e248a2393dd71ee9813d68d800d/Resources/Prototypes/NPCs/Combat/melee.yml
// Licence: MIT, Copyright (c) 2017-2026 Space Wizards Federation; see src/examples/canon/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
// Adapted (YAML prototypes re-written in our domain language).
// Emulations: SS14 `UtilityOperator proto: NearbyMeleeTargets` (alive, visible, distance, health, accessible, in
// line of sight) picks the target while planning; here the host sensor publishes `(hostile ?target)` best-first
// and `melee_target` takes the first. The SS14 `UtilityService` that re-picks the target every tick while the hit
// runs is the host's job too: it rewrites `(hostile ...)` and the agent replans on the change.
// Deviations: the escape rung is one primitive (SS14: `ContainerOperator` then `EscapeOperator`).
// Not ported: the weapon rungs of the ladder (pick up a melee weapon, wield it, switch it on: the creatures here
// fight with their own body; they belong to a `melee_brawler` example), `MeleeAttackOrderedTargetCompound` (orders
// from a leader), `shutdownState: PlanFinished` on the move (SS14 keeps steering towards the target until the plan
// ends; it is the executor's cleanup timing, not a plan end).
//
// Facts:      (hostile ?target) host sensor, best first; (buckled), (pulled), (in_container) body state;
//             (distance_to ?entity ?metres).
// Primitives: (!unbuckle) (!unpull) (!escape_container) (!move_near ?entity ?range) (!juke_away ?target)
//             (!melee_attack ?target)

(:domain melee

    // The target to fight now: the host's best hostile.
    (:axiom (melee_target ?out_target)
        (and
            (hostile ?out_target)
        )
    )

    // Contract: one step towards hitting ?inp_target, or the hit; never fails.
    (:method (melee ?inp_target)

        (unbuckle
            (and
                (buckled)
            )
            (
                (!unbuckle)
            )
        )

        (break_free
            (and
                (pulled)
            )
            (
                (!unpull)
            )
        )

        (escape
            (and
                (in_container)
            )
            (
                (!escape_container)
            )
        )

        (attack
            ()
            (
                (get_in_range ?inp_target @melee_range)
                (!juke_away ?inp_target)
                (!melee_attack ?inp_target)
            )
        )
    )
)
